  m_Name: ArabianOryx
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::WildTamers.Animals.AnimalData
  id: arabian_oryx
  displayName: Arabian Oryx
  styleLabel: Sturdy horn fighter
  description: The Arabian oryx is a pale antelope with two long, straight horns.
    Its white coat reflects the hot sun, and it can live a long time without drinking.
    It walks on wide hooves that suit soft sand.
  history: Desert people hunted the oryx for meat and hide, and it nearly disappeared.
    By 1972 it was gone from the wild. Breeding programmes in zoos saved it, and
    today oryx live again in reserves in Saudi Arabia and Oman.
